Please note that the above code assumes that your ArrayList is a List that maintains the order of elements. If that's not the case, then the assertions might need to be adjusted.
--------------------Here are your assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@":

```cs
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX);
Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
```

These assert statements are checking if the index of the element `x` in the old array is less than or equal to that in the new array. If the element is not present in the new array (i.e. the return value is `false`), then the `IndexOf()` and `LastIndexOf()` methods return -1 which is greater than or equal to any integer, hence this condition will always be true. If the element is present in the new array, then `IndexOf()` and `LastIndexOf()` methods will return a positive integer which is greater than or equal to the index of `x` in the old array.
