Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX <= New_arrListIndexOfX || Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= New_arrListLastIndexOfX);

// @@@ If the return value is true, count of the array before and after the operation is increased by at least 1
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1);

// @@@ If Contains() returns true, the new count of the array should be greater than the old count
Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount > Old_arrListCount);
```

These assertions ensure that the `Contains()` method behaves as expected. The `Contains()` method should return true if and only if `x` is in the list. So, the index of `x` or the last index of `x` should increase or stay the same. Also, the count of the list should increase by at least 1.
